# OpenLive — Caddy reverse proxy template
# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and replace YOUR_DOMAIN with your domain.
# (setup-oracle.sh writes the real file for you — this is just the template.)
# With a domain, Caddy fetches a free HTTPS certificate automatically.

YOUR_DOMAIN {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}

# No domain? Use this instead (plain HTTP on port 80, no HTTPS):
# :80 {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
# }
#
# The backend itself always listens only on 127.0.0.1:8000 — it is
# never exposed directly to the internet. If you bypass Caddy entirely,
# you would use http://<PUBLIC-IP>:8000/ instead, but then you must open
# port 8000 in the firewall and you have no HTTPS at all.
